<!--Post: 3311--><!--Time: 1104781592-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3311"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Lubbock<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Lubbock<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, January 03, 2005 - 11:46 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I am a writer currently working on a second novel, this one concerning a series of undiscovered, unsolved, and unconnected murders set in my geographical area over an eighteen year period. My first book was a political/ espionage/ Appocalyptic thriller in which a serial killer played a small role. I am obsessive in my research in order to craft characters with authenticity. I also have an undergraduate degree in psychology and am a keen observer of human behavior. <BR> <BR>I fell into the black hole of the BTK mystery on or about December 15,2004 as the result of a story on CNN. Although I have a vague reccolection of the case from previous research. this time it really put the hook in me. I deeply appriciate all of the well thought out and insightful commentaries of the contributors to this site. <BR> <BR>Here are some thoughts and observations from my ever-swelling notebook, graded on a scale of 1-5 &#34;&#42;&#34;s with 5 being most probable - &#40;most elements have remained unchanged from the first two days although in perusing the site I&#39;ve come across many independent citings of certain items&#41;:   <BR> <BR>&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42; BTK is slight of build, medium height, wirey and deceptively strong &#40;maybe works out, jogs&#41;. His facial features are unremarkable and unmemorable.  <BR>     - He wears glasses, especially in his advanced age. <BR>     - His voice would&#39;ve changed with age,      &#40;slightly lower in pitch and with a gravelly aspect creeping in&#41;. <BR>     - He may appear the quintessential &#34;nerd&#34;, a charter member of the pocket-protector set. <BR>     - He is not happy with his physical appearance, hence the &#34;Blind&#34; aspect of BTK. &#40;I&#39;ve borrowed this from the novel &#34;Red Dragon&#34; by Thomas Harris; those of you who have read it or seen the movie may recall that the killer breaks mirrors in the victim&#39;s house and impaqles the jagged shards in their eyes&#41;. <BR> <BR>&#42;&#42; He served in Viet Nam &#40;&#34;Born To Kill&#34;&#41; but he was in the rear with the gear, probably as a helicopter of airplane mechanic. He may&#39;ve developed a taste for killing by offing south-east Asain prostitutes. <BR> <BR>&#42;&#42;&#42; He went to college on the G.I. Bill. He changed majors more than once, and may not have completed a degree <BR> <BR>Excuse the non-sequential digression but did the cops dust for prints behind the rear-view mirrors of the Otero and Wegerle &#40;?&#41; vehicles, where one might touch to adjust and then forget to wipe? What was the disposition of those vehicles? <BR> <BR> <BR>Since I&#39;ve never been to Wicita my only assets in sleuthing this matter are the internet and a 2002 Wichita phone directory at the library. Although I admit it&#39;s a long shot, many people use their own first names or a reasonable facsimile thereof when choosing an alias. I studied the &#34;K&#34;s in the phone book, looking for BTK initials &#40;or &#34;William&#34;s&#41;. It would&#39;ve been nice to have mid-seventies directory to cross reference it with, but one of the many tid-bits that came to mind while reviewing my list of names, addresses, and phone numbers was BTK&#39;s reference to &#34;...new vines at night&#34;; it seemed awkward, almost impertinent to the context, i,e: could N. Vine Street have some significance, or am I climbing the left-field wall on that one? <BR> <BR>&#42;&#42;&#42; He drives an earlier model white pick-up truck with a tool box in the bed. <BR> <BR>&#42;&#42;&#42; Hen is sociable on a superficial level, and may have acquaintances but no close friends. His mother died recently. He was living with her and remains in the house. He has no remaining family. <BR> <BR>&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42; He has above average intelligence but was learning disabled &#40;dyslexia?&#41; which in the era he grew up in would&#39;ve labeled him with the short bus syndrome. Maybe he&#39;s not intentionally dumbing down his syntax, grammer and spelling. He does read some - mostly true crime and murder mysteries - but feels more at home with mechanical tinkering. <BR> <BR>&#42;&#42; He has been in Wichita the whole time. Early on, after I&#39;d read a profile of Wichita that listed Boeing as a major industry I&#39;d entertained a notion that he might&#39;ve transferred to Seattle during what may be viewed as his inactive period. This was based on the seemingly disproportionate number of true-crime books that detail events that took place in the Pacific north-west, especially around Seattle &#40;maybe its the gloomy weather?&#41;. I&#39;ve since revised my opinion, and believe that many of the unsolved murders in the general area may someday be attributed to BTK. <BR>     - He has an unsteady work history with periods of under-employment and unemployment. I concur with those who have suggested that at one time he worked for the Coleman Co., possibly in close proximity to Julie Otero and Katheryn Bright. I was also intrigued to learn &#40;if true&#41; that their supervisor, Micheal Williams, was shot four days prior to the Otero murders. <BR>     - That BTK toiled for Olan Mills seems a legitimate possibility. Kudos to whoever it was that pointed out that he had a photo of Ms. Bright prior to the crime, I&#39;d missed that. <BR>     - In the mid seventies he repaired copiers and office machines at WSU, including the library. <BR> <BR>&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42; Although BTK relishes control, he resents that his &#34;true talents and abilities&#34; have never been recognized. He has never risen to a management position. This does not mean he&#39;s not experienced at giving orders - many a peon does not recognize him/herself as such. In his 9-1-1 call on Ms. Fox he was assertive yet courteous, as opposed to coming across as obnoxiously aggressive. He is a no-nonsense and probably humorless person, but has a disarming, curteous charm that can put people at ease. He also carries himself with a condfident demeanor which he can maintain for relatively short periods of time despite a gnawing underlying sense of inferiority. <BR>     - He becomes extremely defensive when questioned or contradicted, which inevitably pushes him down the pecking order in office politics, hence his lack of career advancement. Another inhibiting factor is that he views his employment as secondary to his &#34;art&#34;. <BR> <BR>&#42;&#42; Within the past year he has been diagnosed with prostate cancer. <BR> <BR>&#42;&#42;&#42; His father was a boxer &#40;surmised from baby picture&#41; <BR> <BR>&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42; He frequents parks but avoids the people there. He may photograph birds. He probably dresses down and darkens his skin/hair for forrays into parks in bad neighborhoods. He may appear to be a destitute trash picker &#40;is dumpster-diving against the law up there?&#41; He may climb trees and take pictures through a telephoto lense. <BR> <BR> <BR>Questions: Would he be audacious enough to allow his picture to be posted on a web site &#40;ham radio club, for example&#41;. The in-your-face aspect of it might get him off? <BR> <BR>Are there wooded areas within telescopic range and line of sight from the crime scenes? <BR>I&#39;ve printed off aerial photos but have het to analyze them. <BR> <BR>What are the buildings just west&#40;?&#41; of 3217 E. 13th? <BR> <BR>What is the building directly across the street from 803 N. Edgemoor? Also, there is a cluster of trees behind the residence, does an alley lead through it? <!--/Text--></td></tr>
