<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3313"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Wade<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Wade<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, January 03, 2005 - 12:25 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Lubbock- <BR>A few things that i find aren&#39;t correct as far as facts go. <BR> <BR>1&#41; You refer to the b as being for &#40;blind&#41;....its bind. <BR> <BR>2&#41; His dad was a boxer....deduced from pic of baby...I still have pajamas from childhood..that is a dog on the pic, i have one exactly like it, they are not boxing gloves as i have seen posted before IMO...second..we don&#39;t know if its a pic of BTK or anyone else connected with the case. <BR> <BR>3&#41; Where did the white pick up come from?  I have never seen that mentioned any where. <BR> <BR>4&#41; Prostrate cancer???  How do you surmise that?? <BR> <BR>You may know more than me...I just dont see where some of your info is from. <BR> <BR>Care to share that with us??? <BR>thanks<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3313-->
<!--Post: 3318--><!--Time: 1104792244-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3318"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Armchairpi<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Armchairpi<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, January 03, 2005 - 2:44 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text--><i>Lubbock- <BR>A few things that i find aren&#39;t correct as far as facts go. <BR> <BR>1&#41; You refer to the b as being for &#40;blind&#41;....its bind.</i> <BR> <BR>Took me a minute too, Wade, but then I recalled in one of his letters BTK misspells &#34;bind&#34; as &#34;blind&#34;.  Intentional clue?  Freudian slip?  Just a bad speller? <BR> <BR>It&#39;s in the &#34;Oh Death to Nancy&#34; poem that is in the &#34;Poetry&#34; link on this site: <BR><i>I&#39;ll stuff your jaws till you can&#39;t talk <BR>I&#39;ll blind your leg&#39;s till you can&#39;t walk</i><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3318-->
<!--Post: 3320--><!--Time: 1104795761-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3320"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Lubbock<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Lubbock<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, January 03, 2005 - 3:42 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Wade, <BR>Thanks for the correction, I guess sometimes the mind sees what it wants to see - boy is my face red - almost as bad as when it took me an entire morning to decipher Tom&#39;s seasons greetings to us because I dismissed &#34;holiday&#34; as a possibility because I had a brain spasm and thought it was spelled with two &#34;L&#39;s. <BR> <BR>Also, thanks for the info on the baby&#39;s pjs - the dog wasn&#39;t a boxer was it? &#40;just kidding&#41;. I still think its a solid assumption that it was our subject&#39;s baby picture, however I concede that its not necessarily so. <BR> <BR>As for the pick-up truck, I based that on my over-all impression of BTK as a mechanically inclined, blue-collar jack-of-all-trades type of individual who would be inclined to use the vehicle in relation to legitimate work as well as a commonplace and unremarkable mode of conveyance for stalking and surviellance. White seems to be the most frequently seen color of pick-up down here - especially work related vehicles. I assume he may carry a variety of tools in a built-in, locking chest in the bed, along with his special kit. He may even have an assortment of magnetic signs that he sticks on as the occasion requires. I appoligize if I led you to believe that I was working with anything more substantial than a gut hunch and speculation based on interpretation of the information I&#39;ve gleaned thus far. I doubt that I have access to any information that you don&#39;t. <BR> <BR>I based my speculation that he may have been diagnosed with prostate cancer on the assumption that his sudden re-emergence into the public eye may have been catalyzed by a sudden and catastrophic change of life. Extrapolating upon this theme, there is a strong correlation between high testosterone levels and risk-taking behaviors - especially in relation to sex and violence. There is also a strong correlation between elevated levels of testosterone and prostate cancer. In other words my theory was just another shot in the dark. I was using this forum as a sounding-board, and I deeply appreciate your feedback. I am also well aware of what can happen when one &#34;assume&#34;s.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3320-->
<!--Post: 3339--><!--Time: 1104812778-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3339"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Wade<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Wade<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, January 03, 2005 - 8:26 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Lubbock...thanks for showing me the light on the truck and the prostrate cancer.  I agree both are plausible. <BR>I hope you didn&#39;t think i was dogging you...just thought i could correct a couple of things.  and also wanted to know more on why the truck and cancer.  thank you for your explanation!<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3339-->
<!--Post: 3361--><!--Time: 1104823171-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3361"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Oklahoma_mike<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Oklahoma_mike<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->11-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, January 03, 2005 - 11:19 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Lubbock, I think the idea of prostate cancer is a good example of what could have happened within the past year to drive him out again.  Prostate cancer is often very slow, it can take 10 years to kill somebody and it is not rare for someone to die of something else, like a heart attack, in the meantime!  So that would be a very serious illness but still not totally incapacitated, in that he could usually go about day to day tasks.  Total sexual dysfunction does not always occur with such cancer but it sometimes does.  This could be a reason that he is not trying to kill any more as his sexual function is gone.  If his re-emergence is due to personal illness prostate cancer is a better guess than many.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3361-->
<!--Post: 3371--><!--Time: 1104839277-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3371"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Nugzter<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Nugzter<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, January 04, 2005 - 3:47 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Hey Lubbock,  <BR>intresting stuff. How di you get the idea about the truck with toolbox? Thats a quite detailed assumption. By the way, I grew up in Lubbock, Tx.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3371-->
<!--Post: 3431--><!--Time: 1104891662-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3431"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Q<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Q<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, January 04, 2005 - 6:21 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->He bound them with the cord from blinds<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3431-->
<!--Post: 3474--><!--Time: 1104951261-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3474"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Lubbock<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Lubbock<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, January 05, 2005 - 10:54 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Nugzter, <BR>Hey homeboy. <BR> <BR>Regarding the truck with the toolbox - I based that my impression of BTK as a nuts-and-bolts type guy. As in the development of my fictional characters, I base what an individual is likely to do based on a set of basic and fundimental personality traits. True, we are not certain what parts of his history that he has revealed, if any, is true, however I believe that a good deal of it is. Due to the lack of tracable specifics I believe he is enjoying our futile interpretations of what he has provided. If I know him like I think I do his sense of intellectual superiority is enhanced by providing us lowly mortals with true facts &#40;albeit obscure ones&#41; to tantalize and baffle us. <BR> <BR>That being said I believe that his actions and his need to control and dominate spring from a deep seated inferiority complex that stems from his childhood. Many serial killers come from disfunctional homes with a weak or absent father figure. I believe he wrote that his father was killed in WWII. His mother may have been domineering, maybe even cruel, and I believe that she was hyper-religious and hammered guilt into his young psyche, especially in regard to sexual matters. This is going a bit further out on a limb but he may have been the product of an unexpected and unwanted pregnancy &#40;which his mother may have regarded as a nine-month parasitic infection&#41;, maybe from an affair. He was not close with his grandparents, who were overly strict and judgemental. <BR> <BR>Compounding his sense of being unwanted at home, as I mentioned in an earlier post I believe that he suffered from a learning disability, which caused peers and teachers to regard him as stupid. <BR> <BR>He was probably slow to mature physically and as a result bullied at school and rejected by girls. He most likely was not cute or handsome, and was probably shy. The constant rejection he suffered formed a self-image of being ugly. <BR> <BR>All of the aforementioned factors set the table for what he was to become. <BR> <BR>He is a concrete thinker, which enhances his mechanical abilities, but has trouble with abstract concepts. Artistic endeavors come difficult to him - hence the derivative nature of his poetry. <BR> <BR>His interests: trains, photography, mechanical engineering - all point to a &#34;hands-on&#34; &#34;Mr. Fix it&#34; type individual, as does his claim that he repaired copiers and office machines. This is what led me to believe that he drives a work type vehicle such as a pick-up with a locking tool box in back. My other choice - which I read yesterday in the account of the fireman who witness a man who may have been BTK using a pay phone - was a van or a utility-type panel-truck. Although it wasn&#39;t specified I picture the van as having no windows in the back, and being of an older model, maybe with a few scrapes and dings. The fireman discribed the individual as having blondish hair and wearing a gray work uniform. I can&#39;t remember which thread I saw the link to the article on or I would cite it. <BR> <BR>The crux of the matter is that I take issue with those who suggest that BTK is a succesful and prominent individual; instead, he scrapes by, doing odd jobs between periods of regular employment, and it burns him no end that he is never recognized for his true genius. <BR> <BR>He lives in the house that he inherited from his mother or grandparents. He owns it free and clear, no mortgage payments. He may rent it out during periods that he is out of town, but for the most part he has lived in Wichita the whole time. <BR> <BR>He may own a small fix-it shop, and suppliments his income as a &#34;Honey-do&#34; man. He may be on social security and/or a VA pension. <BR> <BR>He may be married, but if so it is for appearances &#40;a Micheal Jackson type union&#41;, however I suspect he&#39;s a life-long bachelor. <BR> <BR>He&#39;s a binge drinker, but doesn&#39;t imbibe on a daily basis. He may drink alone at home in front of the tube - probably cheap liquor. <BR> <BR>He has a workshop/ darkroom/ dungeon in his house. I wouldn&#39;t be surprised if in a variation of his MOs he abducts prostitutes and/or female hitchhikers to torture and kill at his leasure, and then maybe dump the bodies in a 55 gallon drum filled with cement into the Arkansas river. <BR> <BR>Here are some common characteristics of the &#34;organized killer&#34; &#40;again, I would cite the source but I didn&#39;t record it on my notes&#41;: <BR> <BR>- Craving attention. A sense of being important and larger than life. <BR> <BR>- Fantasy and ritual. <BR> <BR>- Keeps souvineers and/or a scrapbook. <BR> <BR>- Plans crime. <BR> <BR>- Targets a stranger. <BR> <BR>- Personalizes victim. <BR> <BR>- Controls conversation with victim. <BR> <BR>- Demands submissive victim. <BR> <BR>- Restraints. <BR> <BR>- Aggression before death. <BR> <BR>- Transports and hides bodies. <BR> <BR>- Doesn&#39;t leave weapon behind. <BR> <BR>- Average or above intelligence. <BR> <BR>- Socially competent. <BR> <BR>- Skilled work preffered. <BR> <BR>- Sexually competent. <BR> <BR>- High birth order status. <BR> <BR>- Father&#39;s work unstable. <BR> <BR>- Inconsistant childhood discipline. <BR> <BR>- Remains calm during crime. <BR> <BR>- May be substance abuser, especially alcohol. <BR> <BR>- Stressor precipitating act. <BR> <BR>- Living with a partner &#40;I believe he was living with his mother prior to her recent&#40;?&#41;death. <BR> <BR>- Mobile. With vehicle. &#40;I believe he parks on the other side of a park or parking lot and walks a secluded route to the victim&#39;s home&#41;. <BR> <BR>- Follows media. <BR> <BR>- May change jobs, leave town. <BR> <BR>Some of these may or may not apply to BTK. <BR> <BR>Sexual murderers: <BR> <BR>- %72 lacked positive relationship with father figure. <BR> <BR>- %66 had a domineering mother <BR> <BR>- %86 had a psychiatric history. <BR> <BR>- %80 had an unstable work record. <BR> <BR>- %68 were reasonably bright but underachieving. <BR> <BR>- %70 were interested in pornography, voyerism, fetishism. <BR> <BR>E-gads! I&#39;ve just described myself. &#40;JOKE&#41;. <BR>More later.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3474-->
<!--Post: 3477--><!--Time: 1104954179-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3477"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Armchairpi<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Armchairpi<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, January 05, 2005 - 11:42 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Regarding the fireman who saw BTK make the Nancy Fox phone call, see: <BR><a href="http://www.kansas.com/mld/kansas/news/special_packages/btk/archive/8348962.htm" target=_top>http://www.kansas.com/mld/kansas/news/special_pack ages/btk/archive/8348962.htm</a> <BR> <BR>and the march 31, 2004 post by &#34;DWD&#34; at this blog: <a href="http://www.thoughtpeach.com/archives/000411.html" target=_top>http://www.thoughtpeach.com/archives/000411.html</a> <BR> <BR>The blog commenter states that authorities were able to trace the call and essentially &#42;69 it within moments.  If we believe DWD, there is little doubt that the fireman &#42;did&#42; indeed see whoever made the N.F. call &#40;and the caller almost certainly had to be BTK&#41;.  The Eagle article is not specific about how the fireman came forward with his information. <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3477-->
<!--Post: 3481--><!--Time: 1104956120-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3481"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:s.glasscock@sbcglobal.net" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Questions<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Questions<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, January 05, 2005 - 12:15 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I have read an article about this.  The &#34;&#42;69&#34; that the operator did was answered by the fireman waiting for the pay phone because BTK was on it <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3481-->
<!--Post: 3619--><!--Time: 1105065703-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3619"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Whoisbtk<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Whoisbtk<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, January 06, 2005 - 6:41 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Lubbock: <BR> <BR>Maybe I just have a different idea about the purpose of this site, but our fantasies about what BTK might be are going to be as varied as the number of posters.  If you are just spitting back data to get the reaction of this group for use in your next novel, it really feels like you&#39;re using this issue for your own commercial advantage. <BR> <BR>I mean really, where do you have any basis for the binge drinking, to say nothing of the &#34;cheap liquor&#34; part? <BR> <BR>There are eight victim&#39;s families, and a city that is aware of a killer among them, that take this seriously.  Would you mind sharing the basis for some of the things you believe are part of BTK&#39;s makeup? <BR> <BR>Sorry if this is offensive. <BR> <BR>&#40;Tom: I’m new to posting.  This may violate posting rules, sorry if it did.&#41; <BR> <BR><a href="mailto:whoisbtk@yahoo.com">whoisbtk@yahoo.com</a> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3619-->
<!--Post: 3624--><!--Time: 1105070458-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3624"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->George<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->George<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, January 06, 2005 - 8:00 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Whoisbtk: Your post is not offensive, it is cogent. All are entitled to their opinions, of course, and a lengthy list of supposed traits only makes me appreciate Mike Kelleher&#39;s stance that at least some of the old Ressler/Douglas profiling beliefs are simply wide of the mark. <BR> <BR>Interestingly, John Douglas&#39; view that too many serial offenders are released early from prison, and often the fault is that of the jailhouse psychiatrist and/or psychologist. &#34;Fault&#34; in a sense that the final decision of these head doctors is based on &#34;self-reporting&#34; from the prisoner. I pretty much agree with this. <BR> <BR>The thing is, when the early profilers were conducting interviews with serial offenders who were in prison, the profilers had to rely on &#34;self-reporting&#34; as well. Many of the traditional profiling beliefs still have merit, in my opinion, but others don&#39;t. <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3624-->
<!--Post: 3629--><!--Time: 1105073870-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3629"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Whoisbtk<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Whoisbtk<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, January 06, 2005 - 8:57 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->George: 10-4.  I need to re-evaluate the distinction between profiling the criminal and evaluating/reconstructing the crime. <BR> <BR>Lubbock: Seriously, what leads you to the &#34;cheap liquor&#34; part of your profile?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3629-->
<!--Post: 3666--><!--Time: 1105118035-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3666"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Lubbock<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Lubbock<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, January 07, 2005 - 9:13 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Whoisbtk, <BR> <BR>I believe that on occasions when all of the garbage in his tortured psyche backs up on him, especially when frustrated, BTK seeks the relief of oblivion through the bottle. In a situation such as when Anna didn&#39;t appear his methodical nature and finely honed sense of self preservation overcame the internal immature, ego-driven demand for immediate gratification and he resisted perpetrating &#40;I assume&#41; an ill-advised and risky blitz type attack at random. But the &#34;steam&#34; pressure was pushing red-line. Weary of stewing in his own juices he needed an outlet. Being an intensely goal driven individual he&#39;d choose the most effective tool for the job, i.e. hard liquor. Not being an affluent individual, he goes for more bang-for-the-buck, probably congratulating himself for disciplined budgeting and sneering at pretentious fools who might drink Chivas or the like. Drinking helps him relinquish the oppressive burden of having to maintain a regimented sense of control over everything. It breaks set, and in the morning a bit of equalibruim is restored. Also, I believe that by nature he is a solitary person. This doesn&#39;t mean that he&#39;s a hermit - as he is able to socialize effectively in order to maintain himself in society - but his relationships are superficial, and he discloses little of himself to others. I&#39;m fairly certain that he&#39;s never confided his crimes to another living person, and he&#39;d be a firm believer in the old saw that two can keep a secret if one of them&#39;s dead. Booze loosens the tongue. I doubt he&#39;d hang out at the corner bar. And getting arrested, say for a DWI or PI, would definitely put a crimp in his style. <BR> <BR>Make no mistake about it, I would like to see this sick f&#42;&#42;&#42; caught. I have more empathy and caring for the victims and those close to them than you might imagine. Yesterday I spent three hours plus at the library with the Wichita phone book, once again combing the white and yellow pages, cross referencing, looking for specific patterns and trends based upon all I&#39;ve learned over the internet. I have a list of names and in some cases addresses and phone numbers, admittedly many of which, but not all, are related to the possibility of &#34;BTK&#34; being an acronym. One interesting find; under the &#34;handyman&#34; listing in the yellow pages is a business with the same name and phone number as a certain nebulous storage facility inexplicably listed under &#34;railroads&#34;. There are others. <BR> <BR>If I lived in Wichita there are a few individuals that I&#39;d be watching from afar, maybe picking through their trash and looking into the possibility and process of obtaining a DNA sample &#40;maybe saliva from a discarded soda can or cigarette butt&#41;and submitting it to a private lab for testing and then, probably annonymously submitting the results to law enforcement. I&#39;d also try to discretely interview some folks, including any that I could find who worked for Coleman Company in the seventies, maybe Olan Mills, etc. etc. <BR> <BR>As for my using this matter in relation to my writing - I already know who my characters are, where they are going and how they&#39;re going to get there. This obsession is doing nothing but taking away time from the writing; I am a novice at the computer and the internet, and this post was definitely not on my to-do list for this morning. Sure, I may come across a tid-bit here or there that I can use, but the same could be said for every facet of my life - awake or dreaming - and everything and everyone I meet, observe, listen to, taste, touch, or smell. I appoligize if this offends you. <BR> <BR>I admit, my stream-of-consciousness musings may be wrong, in part or in entirity, but I would derive no greater pleasure than finding this anal orifice and beating the holy snot out of him before turning him in; maybe even delivering him up annonymously, hog-tied, on the front stoop of the WPD. As for anyone out there who might take offence to this, spewing bleeding heart drivel like &#34;he&#39;s sick and he needs help&#34; save it for someone who gives a s&#42;&#42;&#42;; its a circus world and I&#39;m an animal. My rights stop at the tip of your nose - don&#39;t push it.    <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3666-->
<!--Post: 3730--><!--Time: 1105161387-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3730"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->George<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->George<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, January 07, 2005 - 9:16 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Who: Your mention of crime scenes reminds me of the importance of geographic profiling. I really think this is one of the ways in which BTK might be apprehended. Geographic profiling, like any serious art, often revises itself as times passes and from what I understand, geographic profilers, their numbers, are increasing. And I like it!<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3730-->
